,0.0,-0.08181456476449966,-0.4600135087966919,0.0,-3.814689989667386e-06,0.0,-0.00823353324085474,-0.2848097085952759,-8.344646857949556e-07,-4.172316494077677e-06,-0.19880221784114838,-0.0005277194431982934,-8.344646857949556e-07,0.0,-3.2186455882765586e-06,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,-0.09572626650333405,-0.4375584125518799,-0.06030817702412605,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-3.814689989667386e-06,0.0,-7.462222856702283e-05,-5.721882189391181e-05,0.0,-4.768360213347478e-06,-1.5258672647178173e-05,-3.099436753473128e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,26972,18267,1786,74263,525,6839,448,400,1867,25,4897,25,6484,284,220,16,25,17,25,18,12947,3555,374,279,11341,315,279,91766,3082,311,279,650,927,14255,3082,304,279,18267,12671,448,23033,400,1808,3,30,17399,697,4226,438,264,4185,19419,13,508,6405,921,474,297,13842,62944,26,1159,17047,26,1379,7,16,20,15,1215,1638,2752,2333,258,28357,7,15,13,23,1106,7559,7633,91958,1188,21,11,15,701,21,11,15,11,16,23,15,29621,21621,317,7559,7633,91958,1188,18,11,15,701,18,11,15,11,16,23,15,29621,21621,11,7559,2752,28,5782,1215,5155,7633,91958,1188,23,11,15,701,17,11,15,11,16,23,15,29621,21621,11,7559,2752,28,5782,1215,5155,7633,91958,1188,16,16,11,15,701,16,11,15,11,16,23,15,29621,21621,11,7559,2752,28,5782,317,1502,20912,32,3,44970,16,17,11,15,701,50,1215,2383,20912,33,3,44970,16,15,11,15,701,50,1215,2383,20912,34,3,44970,21,11,15,701,50,1215,2383,20912,35,3,44970,15,11,15,701,50,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFour semi-circles are shown with $AB:BC:CD = 1:2:3$. What is the ratio of the shaded area to the unshaded area in the semi circle with diameter $AD$? Express your answer as a common fraction. [asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\nfilldraw(arc((6,0),6,0,180)--cycle);\nfilldraw(arc((3,0),3,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white); filldraw(arc((8,0),2,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white); filldraw(arc((11,0),1,0,180)--cycle,fillpen=white);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(12,0),S); label(\"$B$\",(10,0),S); label(\"$C$\",(6,0),S); label(\"$D$\",(0,0),S);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fb8d58c2b8d770c61a8206284ac6247f7884ec57afd574ad5fb7560782d7deb1"},"seconds":40.63463306427002,"seed":715027442938786232,"stop":"eos","text":"Given that $AB:BC:CD = 1:2:3$, we can assign lengths to these segments as follows: $AB = x$, $BC = 2x$, and $CD = 3x$. Therefore, the total length $AD = AB + BC + CD = x + 2x + 3x = 6x$.\n\nThe area of a semi-circle is given by $\\frac{1}{2}\\pi r^2$, where $r$ is the radius of the semi-circle. \n\nThe semi-circle with diameter $AD$ has a radius of $3x$, so its area is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\pi (3x)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi 9x^2 = \\frac{9}{2} \\pi x^2\n\\]\n\nThe semi-circles with diameters $AB$, $BC$, and $CD$ have radii $x$, $2x$, and $3x$ respectively, so their areas are:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\pi (x)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi x^2, \\quad \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (2x)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi 4x^2 = 2 \\pi x^2, \\quad \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (3x)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi 9x^2 = \\frac{9}{2} \\pi x^2\n\\]\nSince the semi-circles with diameters $AB$, $BC$, and $CD$ are unshaded and subtracted from the semi-circle with diameter $AD$, the total unshaded area is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\pi x^2 + 2 \\pi x^2 + \\frac{9}{2} \\pi x^2 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2} + 2 + \\frac{9}{2}\\right) \\pi x^2 = \\left(\\frac{1 + 4 + 9}{2}\\right) \\pi x^2 = 7 \\pi x^2\n\\]\n\nThe shaded area is the area of the large semi-circle minus the unshaded area:\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{2} \\pi x^2 - 7 \\pi x^2 = \\frac{9}{2} \\pi x^2 - \\frac{14}{2} \\pi x^2 = -\\frac{5}{2} \\pi x^2 = \\frac{5}{2} \\pi x^2\n\\]\n\nThe ratio of the shaded area to the unshaded area is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{5}{2} \\pi x^2}{7 \\pi x^2} = \\frac{5}{14}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the shaded area to the unshaded area is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{5}{14}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{5}{14}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
